  "limitations": [
    "The 32-bit x87 control-word assembly is a no-op on the x64/SSE build; the compiler and native bridge use precise floating-point mode instead.",
    "Sys_Error returns a fatal MiniLang error for the outer host lifecycle to shut down instead of owning a recursive MessageBox/60-second console wait and calling exit directly.",
    "The original WinMain body is split between sys_win.WinMain and host.run so the host loop remains MiniLang-owned; the pinned differential and focused tests cover the system policy, while process-level shutdown remains a separate host gate."
  ]
